  "body": "## What changed\n\n- #2831: 2D Operations explains arc turns on Face, 2D Contour and Slot. It gives the automatic radius and the limits for an explicit radius.\n- #2964: Wire and Sinker EDM lists the four measured QN2 thicknesses and offsets. It explains which offset the post uses to check corners.\n- #2968: Wire and Sinker EDM explains which inside corners, joins and leads a modeled punch can use.\n- #2969: Wire and Sinker EDM explains how to select a convex through-opening and how the post checks the inward lead and retained plate.\n- #2972: Wire and Sinker EDM explains the cut side, air endpoints, clamping and centering confirmations for a straight cutoff.\n- #2974: Wire and Sinker EDM explains how to post two separately captured punches with clear cutting areas.\n- #2978: Wire and Sinker EDM explains DXF chain selection, entry limits and nominal G03 arcs for a circle or racetrack.\n- #2979: Wire and Sinker EDM explains the CCB035 condition, its speed option and the five-pass control check.\n- Posting links to the native wire EDM section.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe site omitted the arc-turn controls and described only a single vertical punch for the native post.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed with zero Rust steps.\n- `zola --root site build` passed. It built 50 pages and 10 sections.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v` ran 104 tests. The link and anchor checks passed.\n- The same three checks failed on upstream/main at `f19ca562b` and on this branch. Both first-part guides reference the removed `tool_library.rs` path for `New tool…`. The site and app license notices also differ.\n- This documentation patch adds no runtime behavior. A regression pin and mutation run do not apply.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNo golden files changed. The site verification built the guide and checked its operation references.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThis patch changes guide text only. Controller runs, Cargo Clippy, heavy lanes and the app example catalog were outside this batch.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#3103 touches the same file, different section (Bore). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3909\n",
